{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Those who say no savior will come to Israel, they console Israel's enemies in vain. Therefore Israel departed and fled from Jerusalem before the Hasmonean wars, and they would answer those who asked: Why do you flee? — For there is no shepherd for Israel, from Israel [i.e., from among themselves]."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The comment reads 'כי' as the object of the preceding question; the final phrase 'מישראל' is hyper-literal and may indicate a textual crux."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:36.277942396Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}